        "description": "At approximately 8:35 a.m. EDT (1235 UTC) on June 30, 2026, NASA astronauts Chris Williams and Jessica Meir will venture outside the International Space Station for an approximately six-and-a-half-hour spacewalk. The pair will replace a wrist joint on the orbital complex’s Canadarm2 robotic arm.\n\nThis spacewalk will be the second for Williams and the fifth for Meir. Williams will serve as spacewalk crew member 1 and will wear a suit with red stripes. Meir will serve as crew member 2 and will wear an unmarked suit.\n\nLearn more about this spacewalk: https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasa-to-cover-us-spacewalk-95-host-preview-news-conference/\nRead the latest mission updates from the station: https://nasa.gov/blogs/spacestation/\n\nCredit: NASA",
